id: position-rowid-off
language: SQL
severity: error
rule:
  pattern: CREATE TABLE positions($$$)
  not:
    pattern: CREATE TABLE positions($$$) WITHOUT ROWID
message: |
  Positions table must use WITHOUT ROWID for composite key performance.
  
  Composite primary key (user_id, market_id, outcome) benefits from
  WITHOUT ROWID optimization in SQLite:
  • No separate ROWID column (saves 8 bytes per row)
  • Primary key becomes the clustered index
  • Faster lookups for composite keys
  
  Always use:
  CREATE TABLE positions(
    user_id TEXT,
    market_id TEXT,
    outcome INT,
    ...,
    PRIMARY KEY (user_id, market_id, outcome)
  ) WITHOUT ROWID;
note: |
  WITHOUT ROWID is critical for tables with:
  • Composite primary keys
  • High read/write ratio
  • Need for space efficiency
  
  Saves ~30% storage and improves lookup speed 2×

